# Godot 4.7

- Engine is Godot 4.7 stable. GDScript is typed (`var n: int`, explicit returns). The project renderer is GL Compatibility.
- `scripts/core/` extends `RefCounted` only. No `Node`, scenes, `get_node`, or `Input` there.
- `scripts/view/` is rendering and input. Static layout lives in `.tscn`. Read nodes with `%UniqueName` and `@onready`. Do not build UI in code.
- The root viewport is 2560×1440. Stretch is `canvas_items` with aspect `expand`, fractional scale, and hidpi on. The window is resizable. The top bar is anchored to the full width and shows `%ManaLabel` (`Mana: N (+M/turn)`) and the turn (`Turn` plus `%TurnLabel` `N / turn_limit`). `camera.default_zoom` is 0.72 so the map fills that window. Do not hardcode the window size in scripts.
- Repeated controls are instanced scenes. `scenes/ui/menu_button.tscn` is the menu button.
- Tunables live only in `config/game_config.json`. `GameConfig.load_file()` push_errors and quits when a key is missing or mistyped. Restart loads the file again.
- Hex math is axial `(q, r)` in `scripts/core/hex.gd`. `+q` is east, `+r` is southeast. The `TileMapLayer` uses odd-r offset: `TILE_SHAPE_HEXAGON`, `TILE_LAYOUT_STACKED`, `TILE_OFFSET_AXIS_HORIZONTAL`.
- Tile size and texture origin live only on `assets/art/bebop_tileset.tres`: face `(128, 108)`, region `(128, 116)`, `texture_origin (0, -4)`. The art is already isometric. Do not squash it and do not copy those numbers into config or scripts.
- Hover uses `TileMapLayer.local_to_map` on that TileSet. `Hex.pixel_to_hex` must keep matching it. The highlight texture is `assets/art/tile_highlight.png`.
- New Game calls `GameSetup.start`. `map.seed` 0 rolls a seed and prints `map seed: N`. Map generation, starts, players, fog, movement, founding, city turns, combat, mana, and spells live in `scripts/core/` (`map_generator.gd`, `map_state.gd`, `player_state.gd`, `fog_state.gd`, `game_setup.gd`, `pathfinder.gd`, `map_city.gd`, `city_rules.gd`, `combat.gd`, `spells.gd`). `CityRules` is yield, growth, and border math. `CityRules.city_mana` is the per-city mana rate. `PlayerState.mana` is the pool, starting at `players.starting_mana`. `Combat` is the damage formula. `SpellRules` is spell area, range, and reject reasons. `GameSetup` applies the queue, healing, attacks, mana income, and casts. `players.starting_units` is settler then warrior. The settler takes the start tile. Each later unit takes the nearest free passable tile, because a tile holds one unit.
- `GameSetup.spawn_unit(player, type, pos)` is the only unit constructor. `pos` is an odd-r offset cell. Pathfinding stays axial inside `Pathfinder` and converts at the `GameSetup` boundary.
- Fog is per player: unrevealed, revealed, visible. Do not paint a land atlas on an unrevealed cell. Dim only revealed-but-not-visible land. Unit vision is `fog.unit_vision`. City vision is the territory radius plus `fog.city_vision_beyond_border`. Units are instances of `scenes/actors/unit.tscn` under the y-sorted `Actors` node, placed with `map_to_local`, tinted with `assets/art/team_tint.gdshader`. Each sprite sits on the cell center. `scenes/actors/hp_bar.tscn` is the HP bar and hides when max HP is 0. Hide units on tiles the viewer cannot currently see. Draw a rival city, and the border segments of an owned tile, once that tile has been explored.
- Found City is `%FoundCityButton` in `scenes/game.tscn` (hotkey `found_city`, B). `%FoundCityReason` shows the core reason while the button is disabled. Move highlights, city markers, border segments, and building markers are instances of `scenes/view/move_highlight.tscn`, `city_marker.tscn`, `border_segment.tscn`, and `building_marker.tscn`. The highlight sprite offset is read from the TileSet. `players.city_names` is one non-empty name list per player.
- `%CityPanel` opens when the human left-clicks their city. It shows food, production, mana from that city, the growth bar, the border clock, and the production queue. That mana line is `CityRules.city_mana`, the same number `GameSetup.mana_per_turn` sums into the top bar. Build buttons are `menu_button` instances. Queue rows are `scenes/ui/queue_row.tscn`. A building is queued by clicking its button, then a highlighted border tile that is not the center. Details are in `docs/cities.md`.
- Left click selects the human unit on that tile. A city on that tile comes after the unit. Right click on a visible enemy attacks. Right click on an empty highlighted tile moves. Attack highlights are red; move highlights stay green. `%SkipButton` / `skip_unit` (S) and `%FortifyButton` / `fortify_unit` (F) are the orders. `%CombatPreview` shows damage and counter-damage. Enter (`end_turn`) ends the turn through the same path as `%EndTurnButton`. The first press warns when a human unit still has moves and no order; the second confirms. End Turn resolves every city's growth, production, and border claim, then adds each player's snapshotted city mana to that player's pool, heals idle units, ticks spell cooldowns, then increments the turn and refills movement. A Mana Well finished this turn is paid on the next End Turn. Enter does nothing while the in-game menu is open. Details are in `docs/combat.md` and `docs/cities.md`.
- `%SpellBar` / `%SpellButtons` sit under the top bar. Buttons are instances of `scenes/ui/spell_button.tscn`, one per config spell. A button's mana check reads `PlayerState.mana` through `GameSetup.spell_block_reason`. Click a ready spell to target. Highlights reuse `scenes/view/move_highlight.tscn` and show the exact radius or line in the new land's color. Left-click casts. Right-click or Esc cancels targeting; Esc toggles the menu only when no spell is armed. `spells.spells_require_revealed_target` rejects an unrevealed tile. Explored and visible both count as revealed. Details are in `docs/spells.md`.
- Commit `.import` and `.uid` files. Do not commit `.godot/`.
- A fresh checkout has no class cache. Run `godot --headless --path . --import` before tests or the game.
- Tests, from the repo root: `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/run_tests.gd`, then the missing-key script (it must exit non-zero), then `--quit-after 120` on `res://scenes/main_menu.tscn` and `res://scenes/game.tscn`, then `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/smoke_game.gd`.
- If you change architecture, conventions, or these commands, update `AGENTS.md`, this file, and `docs/`.
